AGENT_REF = r'''# awt agent reference

Lookup only. Search for the refusal text or the verb. Commands run from the task root as `./awt`.

## Which command

| Situation | Command |
|---|---|
| Starting, not a subagent | `./awt resume` |
| Need to know if it is already recorded | `./awt find "term"` |
| Related decisions, answers and notes from every workspace | `./awt find --like "a sentence"` (`decide` and `ask` list them too) |
| List one kind of thing | `./awt list refs` (also context docs outbox misc decisions questions effects notes state) |
| See old/superseded/answered/terminal items | `./awt list decisions --all` |
| Small fact for later, not a decision | `./awt note "text"` |
| Choice that replaces an earlier choice | `./awt decide "new" --why "r" --supersedes d-7f3a9c21` |
| Choice every later agent must obey | `./awt decide "..." --why "..." --tag rule` |
| Text too long for a field | Write `docs/<name>.md`, then reference its path in the field |
| Slack/chat you can only see pasted | `./awt capture --from slack --title "t" notes.txt` |
| Same content on stdin | `./awt capture --from slack --title "t" -` |
| Doc replaced by a better one | `mkdir -p docs/_superseded && mv -n docs/old.md docs/_superseded/ && test ! -e docs/old.md` (a name already taken there stays put: rename first), then `./awt note "docs/new.md replaces docs/old.md: r"` |
| About to send something that must not go out twice | `./awt effect plan`, `begin`, send it yourself, `mark` (below) |
| Effect stuck `begun` or `unknown` | `./awt effect show <id>`, then ask a person |
| Check workspace health | `./awt doctor` |
| Commit the task dir (person asked) | `git add -A && git commit -m "message"` (`awt doctor --staged` checks for secrets) |
| Task finished | `./awt status done` |

## Syntax

```
./awt state --now "T" --next "T" [--scope S]
./awt note "T"
./awt decide "CHOICE" --why "T" [--supersedes ID] [--tag T]...
./awt ask "T"
./awt answer q-1a2b3c4d "T"
./awt ref TARGET --title "T" [--why "T"] [--kind K] [--no-access]
./awt capture --from SRC --title "T" [--ref URL] [FILE]
./awt status active|paused|done
./awt find "term"
./awt effect plan --target T [--body FILE] [--how TEXT] [--after ID]... [--again] [--why T]
./awt effect begin ID
./awt effect mark ID sent [--ref URL] | not-sent --why T | unknown --why T | dropped
./awt effect show ID
```

The effect ledger is optional. It records a send so it is not made twice. The tool never runs the command: you send with your own tools, and your host's permission system sees the real command.

```
./awt effect plan --target "slack:#eng" --body outbox/release-note.md --how 'slack-cli post "#eng" < outbox/release-note.md'
./awt effect begin e-3c91d0aa        # claims it; print the body path and the mark command
(send it with your own tools)
./awt effect mark e-3c91d0aa sent --ref https://example.slack.com/archives/C1/p1
```

States: `planned` -> `begun` -> `sent`. A failed send: `mark not-sent --why T` (back to `planned`, next attempt). Not sure what happened: `mark unknown --why T`. `--how` is the intended command as text; it is never run. Each `plan` prints the exact next command: copy it.

## Refusals

Every refusal prints `error:` and `fix:`. Read the `fix:` first.

| Refusal | Meaning | Do |
|---|---|---|
| Text over cap | Field too long. Nothing was written. | Write detail to `docs/<name>.md`; put a short summary and the path in the field. Do not split into many rows. |
| Empty text | Blank after strip. | Supply text. |
| Identical state | `state` for that scope matches the current one. | Nothing to record. Move on. If work changed, say what changed. |
| Secret match (names a pattern) | A field holds a credential. Nothing written. No bypass exists. | Remove the secret, refer to it by name or location. If you cannot tell where it is, STOP and ask a person. |
| Unknown id (exit 4) | Wrong id for `answer`, `--supersedes`, `--after`, `effect`. | `./awt list <section>` and copy the id. |
| Already answered / already superseded | Duplicate action. | Use the current id the `fix:` names. |
| Removed flag or `effect apply` (exit 2) | The tool no longer runs commands. | Send it yourself; use `plan`, `begin`, `mark`. |
| Path escapes the root | `--body` path resolves outside the task dir. | Copy the file into `outbox/` or `docs/` and retry. |
| `begin`: not planned | The effect is `begun`, `unknown`, `sent` or `dropped`. | `effect show <id>`. Never send it again. |
| `begin`: someone else is sending | Another process holds the claim. | Wait; check `effect show`. |
| `begin`: body changed | Body file edited after planning. | Re-plan. Show the person the new body. |
| `begin`: `--after` not sent | A prerequisite is not `sent`. | Resolve that effect first. |
| `plan`: open `unknown` on target | An earlier send on this target may have happened. | STOP and ask a person. Do not add `--again`. |
| `plan`: same key, dropped | Person dropped this exact send. | Only if a person wants it again: `--again`. |
| `status done` refused | Lists open questions and effects (`planned`, `begun`, `unknown`). | Resolve each. For questions, a person must answer. For `unknown`, STOP and ask. Never mark `sent` or `dropped` to get past it. |
| Exit 3 | No write permission. | Give the printed command to a person. |
| Exit 4, no `.awt/` | Not in a task. | `cd` to the task dir or pass `--dir`. Do not run `init` unless told. |

## Effect states

| State | You may | You must not |
|---|---|---|
| `planned` | `begin` it, then send; `mark dropped` if it is cancelled | Send without `begin` when a person asked for the ledger |
| `begun` | Send (once) only if you ran `begin` yourself in this session; otherwise treat it as unknown and ask a person. Then `mark sent`, `not-sent --why` or `unknown --why` | Begin again; leave it unmarked |
| `sent` | Proceed; cite `--ref` if known | Plan the same send again |
| `unknown` | Run `effect show <id>`, report to a person, wait for them | Resend. Plan on that target. Mark it yourself. Run `status done`. |
| `dropped` | Move on | Revive without a person asking |

`begun` with no mark stays `begun`: it cannot know whether the send happened, so it never retries and never times out. `status done` is refused until it is marked. `unknown` means the message may already be out. Only a person who has checked the real target may mark an `unknown` effect `sent` or `not-sent`. `not-sent` makes it `planned` again for another attempt.

`--again` is not a retry. It creates a new, separate send that bypasses the duplicate check. A failed or `unknown` send is never retried with `--again`. Use it only when a person wants a deliberate second identical message.

## Subagents

Worker, with a brief:
- Skip `./awt resume`. Read the brief.
- Write output to `docs/<brief>.out.md`. Never name a file starting with REPORT, SUMMARY, FINDINGS or ANALYSIS: Claude Code refuses those for subagents.
- Use `note`, `decide`, `ref`, `capture`, `ask`: parallel writes are safe.
- Do not run `state` or `status`. Do not write a handoff.
- Use `effect` only if the brief says so, and send only when it says so.

Orchestrator:
- Owns `state` and `status`. Run `./awt state` once after collecting worker output, with `--next` naming the next step.
- Links worker files from `state` text by path (`docs/<brief>.out.md`).

## Big tasks: relay

If `./relay` exists and the work splits into parts, do not run them all in one session. Write a plan file (`./relay help` shows the format) with small units, a cheap model for reading, and a `check` command wherever a test can decide. Show the person the plan and `./relay run <plan>`, then stop. Afterwards `./awt resume` shows the result. Workers plan and mark, and send only when their unit says so.

## Wrong moves

- Editing or deleting anything under `.awt/`. Use verbs. A bad row is quarantined, not fatal.
- Copying a page or thread you can link: use `ref`. Use `capture` only when no link works.
- Writing a second handoff such as `docs/HANDOFF.md`. `state` is the handoff.
- Putting long text in `--now`, `--why`, `note`. Write `docs/`, reference the path.
- Using `--again` or a fresh `plan` to get around an `unknown` effect.
- Re-asking or re-researching without `./awt find` first.'''

